PART 4: NET RETURN COMPARISON
==================================================

This is one of the most important features.

The problem we want to solve is that farmers may compare mandi prices without considering all the expenses required to sell their crops.

Build a selling comparison tool that calculates the estimated amount remaining after the entered selling costs.

Inputs:

- Crop name.
- Total quantity in quintals.
- Selling option or mandi.
- Buyer name, if applicable.
- Offered price per quintal.
- Transportation costs.
- Loading and unloading costs.
- Labour expenses.
- Packaging expenses.
- Applicable commission.
- Other selling expenses.
- Optional additional costs.

Allow the farmer to compare multiple selling options.

Calculations:

Gross Sale Value = Quantity × Price Per Quintal

Total Expenses = Sum of All Entered Applicable Expenses

Estimated Net Return = Gross Sale Value − Total Expenses

Estimated Net Return Per Quintal = Estimated Net Return ÷ Quantity

The interface must display:

- Selling price.
- Gross sale value.
- Transportation expenses.
- Other expenses.
- Total expenses.
- Estimated net return.
- Estimated net return per quintal.
- Difference compared with other selling options.

Highlight the option with the highest valid estimated net return.

Allow farmers to edit their assumptions and recalculate the results.

Validate inputs and prevent invalid quantities, division by zero, and negative expense values where inappropriate.

Avoid double-counting any expense.

Clearly label results as estimates based on entered values.

